## 2. VECTOR I: THE SORTIE A/B PROCUREMENT CRUCIBLE & HHI ANTI-MONOCULTURE PORTFOLIO (`INVARIANT 1 & 29`)

### 2.1 The Mechanistic Mismatch: Ex-Ante Standardization as a Single Point of Failure (SPOF)
Legacy defense acquisition (e.g., US DoD JCIDS or prime-contractor block buys) attempts to select a single "winning" drone archetype *ex-ante* and standardize production across $10,000\text{--}100,000$ identical units. Under **Ashby’s Law of Requisite Variety (`Invariant 1`)**, hardware and model standardization in an adversarial theatre creates catastrophic correlated tail risk:
1. **Zero-Day Cyber / Weight Contagion:** If all nodes share an identical flight controller, radio stack, or neural network weight matrix $\mathbf{W}_{\text{Mono}}$, a single captured airframe allows the adversary to synthesize one adversarial optical patch or one protocol exploit that neutralizes $100\%$ of the fleet simultaneously.
2. **Purpose-Built EW Tuning:** When a swarm emits a uniform acoustic harmonic, radar cross-section (RCS), or frequency-hopping pattern, adversary EW guilds rapidly tune notch jammers and point-defense fire-control filters specifically to that single archetype.

### 2.2 The OPSTACK Isomorphism: Thompson-Sampled Sortie Markets & Markowitz Diversity Caps
Rather than treating procurement as a static multi-year contract, sovereign defense logistics must operate as an **automated daily Multi-Armed Bandit / Thompson Sampling market** across $M$ independent micro-foundries, garage fabricators, and e-waste silicon salvagers (`Invariant 27`):

1. **Herfindahl-Hirschman Index (HHI) Anti-Monoculture Constraint:**
   For any sortie wave $t$ composed of $M$ distinct hardware/guidance genotypes with allocation shares $s_{i,t} \in [0, 1]$ ($\sum_{i=1}^M s_{i,t} = 1$), bounding the maximum single-archetype share to $s_{\max,t} = \max_i(s_{i,t}) \le 0.15$ deterministically guarantees that portfolio concentration satisfies:
   $$s_{\max,t} \le 0.15 \implies \text{HHI}_t = \sum_{i=1}^M s_{i,t}^2 \le s_{\max,t} \sum_{i=1}^M s_{i,t} \le 0.15$$
   No single vendor, processor architecture, or sensor model may ever exceed $15\%$ of a deployed wave, guaranteeing that a specialized adversary EW countermeasure can degrade at most $15\%$ of any sortie.

2. **Sub-24-Hour Bayesian Thompson Sampling Feedback Loop (Standoff Overseer + OOB Terminal Confirmation):**
   Each genotype $i$ maintains a Beta posterior distribution $\text{Beta}(\alpha_{i,t}, \beta_{i,t})$ over its empirical penetration/survival yield per dollar expended. Because terminal effector nodes operate in strict RF silence (`Invariant 18`) and are expended on impact, terminal attribution does not rely on the effector transmitting a survival telemetry packet. Instead, **Non-Expendable Standoff Overseers** (`Vector II`) and **Out-of-Band (OOB) Terminal Event Confirmers**—measuring time-gated thermal bloom, acoustic detonation shockwaves, and the sudden flatlining of target RF emitters ($P_{\text{Tx}} \to 0\text{ W}$)—deterministically match each confirmed terminal effect to the trajectory slot and genotype $i$ assigned to that window. These cryptographic state commits update $(\alpha_{i,t+1}, \beta_{i,t+1})$ after each daily wave. Manufacturing bounties for Wave $t+1$ (bounded above the thermodynamic floor, `Invariant 29`) are automatically allocated proportionally to Thompson samples $\theta_{i} \sim \text{Beta}(\alpha_{i,t}, \beta_{i,t})$, reserving an explicit exploration floor ($\epsilon_{\text{explore}} \ge 0.20$) for newly mutated airframe/guidance genotypes.

3. **Thermodynamic Percolation & Ballistic Decoy Homogenization:**
   Within each wave, a fraction $\rho_{\text{decoy}} \in [0.60, 0.85]$ consists of ultra-low-cost, zero-compute mechanical gliders or acoustic/corner-reflector decoys engineered to match the exterior thermal/radar cross-section of compute-bearing nodes (`SPEC-2026-HVT-GAME-THEORETIC-GROUND-DEFENSE-v2.7` Zero-Anomaly Signature Homogenization). The defender's classifier faces maximum Shannon entropy ($\mathcal{H} \to \max$), forcing the expenditure of $\$100\text{K}\text{--}\$1\text{M}$ SHORAD interceptors against $\$50$ decoys.

