## 4. VECTOR III: GROUND-CLUTTER DOPPLER NOTCH STASIS & NANOWATT TICK THERMODYNAMICS (`INVARIANT 14`)

### 4.1 The Mechanistic Mismatch: Gravity Loiter Bleed & Pulse-Doppler MTI Vulnerability
Legacy airborne platforms stay aloft while searching for state transitions, burning $150\text{W}\text{--}1,500\text{W}$ continuously to fight gravity. This limits operational persistence to $30\text{--}90$ minutes and keeps the airframe moving through open sky with a non-zero radial velocity ($v_r > 5\text{ m/s}$) and spinning rotor blades (high micro-Doppler modulation)—placing the platform squarely inside the detection window of modern Pulse-Doppler Moving Target Indicator (MTI) air-defense radars. Meanwhile, academic "tree-branch perching claws" add fragile mechanical weight that fails in mud, wind, or rubble.

### 4.2 The OPSTACK Isomorphism: Zero-Moving-Parts Ground Stasis inside the Radar Clutter Notch
Every modern air-defense radar (e.g., Pantsir, Tor, Patriot, Sentinel) employs a **Doppler Clutter Notch Filter** that deletes radar returns with near-zero radial velocity ($|v_r| < v_{\text{notch}} \approx 2.5\text{--}4.0\text{ m/s}$) to prevent swaying trees, rocks, and buildings from saturating the display.

1. **Flat Ground/Rubble Deposition (Zero Mechanical Grippers):**
   Rather than loitering in the air or using fragile robotic claws, nodes infiltrate during periods of weather clutter or EW blindness and simply land flat on open dirt, gravel, tall grass, rubble, or flat industrial roofs along expected transit corridors days or weeks in advance.
2. **Doppler & Thermal Vanishing ($P_{\text{Propulsion}} = 0.0\text{ W}$):**
   Once on the ground with rotors stopped, radial velocity is strictly zero ($v_r = 0\text{ m/s} < v_{\text{notch}}$), rotor micro-Doppler vanishes, and thermal exhaust equilibrates to ambient soil temperature within minutes. To a $\$100\text{M}$ airborne or ground pulse-Doppler radar, the node is mathematically indistinguishable from a dirt clod.
3. **Milliwatt/Microwatt Interrupt Stasis, Anti-Materiel BFT Signature Gate, & CCW Art. 5 Self-Deactivation Horizon (`Invariant 14 & 17`):**
   Rather than expending $150\text{--}1,500\text{ W}$ in continuous aerodynamic hover, a grounded node unpowers primary propulsion and high-draw compute, maintaining only a low-power wake-on-threshold comparator ($P_{\text{Sleep}} \le 25\text{ mW}$, or $\le 50\,\mu\text{W}$ deep-RTC trigger). From a $50\text{ Wh}$ energy reservoir at $P_{\text{Sleep}} = 25\text{ mW}$ (or a dedicated $50\text{ mWh}$ backup stasis capacitor at $25\,\mu\text{W}$), theoretical stasis endurance scales as $\tau_{\text{Stasis}} = E_{\text{Stasis}} / P_{\text{Sleep}} = 2,000\text{ hours}$ ($> 1,000\text{ hours}$). Strictly compliant with the **Ottawa Convention** and **CCW Amended Protocol II Art. 5**, grounded stasis nodes are **never** victim-activated by human presence; they wake **exclusively** upon local multi-node BFT quorum confirmation (`Invariant 17`) of validated anti-radiation/anti-materiel military signatures (e.g., high-wattage air-defense radar emissions or armored vehicle acoustic/RF profiles under Art. 52(2)) and enforce a hard-wired RTC **Self-Deactivation & Safe-Passivation Horizon** ($\tau_{\text{Stasis}} \le \tau_{\text{SelfDeactivate}}$) that permanently zeroes activation buses upon timer expiry or low-voltage threshold decay.

